	<key>Start the timer from the Wakely menu and your Mac goes to sleep %1$@ later. The menu shows the minutes left; choose the row again to cancel. Over the last minute the sound fades out, and the volume comes back where it was when your Mac wakes or when you cancel. At the end, Wakely turns off and puts your Mac to sleep, even if other apps would keep it awake. If something still keeps it awake 30 seconds later, a notification names it.</key>
